  "Question": "If \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are digits for which \\[ \\begin{array}{r} 2a\\\\[-2pt] {}\\times b3\\\\ \\hline 69\\\\ 92\\phantom0\\\\ \\hline 989 \\end{array} \\] then \\(a+b=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(9\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The first partial product comes from multiplying the top two-digit number by the units digit \\(3\\). Thus the top number is\n\\[\n69\\div3=23,\n\\]\nwhich gives \\(a=3\\).\n\nThe second partial product is shifted one place to the left because \\(b\\) is the tens digit. Its unshifted value is \\(92\\), so\n\\[\nb=92\\div23=4.\n\\]\nThese digits agree with the final product, since \\(23\\times43=69+920=989\\). Therefore \\(a+b=3+4=7\\), choice C.",
